# In-game Basic text

Basic tooltip copy is owned in `tools/community/move_descriptions.json`. Do not invent it. Do not copy Serebii, Bulbapedia, or similar sites as the live source. The Serebii scraper is retired.

UNITE-DB Basic is often a pre-evolution leftover, unofficial, upgrade-only, or the same as Advanced numbers. The owned archive wins over UNITE-DB Basic when it has a real body. Prefer operator-supplied in-game text or tooltip stills. Advanced stays UNITE-DB `rsb.true_desc` (and staged `passive2_description` / `passive3_description`). When Basic already has an Upgrade paragraph, keep it — do not replace it with Advanced.

Do not restore a Game8 ingest, crawler, or cache. Do not copy fan-site Effect / How to Use / strategy prose as the live source.

There is no official Nintendo/TiMi gamemaster API. `uniteapi.dev` is match analytics, not constants. First-party APK datamining is blocked (rotated Unity XOR keys). Do not reverse `libil2cpp.so`, dump APKs, or write decrypt tools. Agents cannot operate a Switch or a UNITE client from this session.

## Apply in-game Basic

1. Put the exact in-game Basic under `move_descriptions.json` → `descriptions.<id>.<normalized name>`. Use `\n\n` between mechanical beats in move bodies. Upgrade stays its own paragraph.
2. If the app still shows a pre-evolution Ability, add that Pokémon's UNITE-DB `name` slug to `PLAYABLE_PASSIVE_SLUGS` in `normalize.py`. Never add `mew` (`passive2` is Move Reset). Never add mega-license slugs (those use `mega_license_passive_names` → Pre-Mega + Mega rows).
3. Drop or retarget `patch_note_overrides.json` entries whose `move` id was the old Ability (unknown ids fail normalize).
4. `npm run data:refresh -- --mode curate --no-verify`, then `python3 tools/community/fetch_art.py`. Do **not** run a full harvest for a description-only pass. Harvest is add-only (it never overwrites an existing archive body).
5. Assert name + a distinctive Basic phrase in `patchBundle.test.ts`. Do not snapshot the full sentence.

Tooltip stills: `tools/community/_descs/<pokemon-id>/`. Transcribe from those pixels into the archive. Do not hand-edit `src/data/patch-current.json`.

Longer sourcing notes: `docs/13-in-game-basic-text.md`.
